    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">As of March 31, 2026, Account 146, Accounts receivable from associated companies, included $232,109,650 of income tax receivable from Berkshire Hathaway Energy Company, PacifiCorp's indirect parent company.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">As of December 31, 2025, Account 146, Accounts receivable from associated companies, included $95,246,799 of income tax receivable from Berkshire Hathaway Energy Company, PacifiCorp's indirect parent company.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">As of December 31, 2025, Account 236, Taxes accrued, included $14,426,715 of income tax payable to Berkshire Hathaway Energy Company, PacifiCorp's indirect parent company.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Depreciation expense associated with transportation equipment is generally charged to operations and maintenance expense and construction work in progress. During the three-month period ended March 31, 2026 and 2025, depreciation expense associated with transportation equipment was $6,197,773 and $5,732,876, respectively.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Generally, PacifiCorp records the depreciation expense of asset retirement obligations as a regulatory asset.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Payroll taxes are generally charged to operations and maintenance expense and construction work in progress. During the three-month periods ended March 31, 2026 and 2025, payroll taxes were $14,848,259 and $15,860,676, respectively.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Generally, PacifiCorp records the accretion expense of asset retirement obligations as a regulatory asset.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The balance in Account 215.1, Appropriated retained earnings - Amortization reserve, Federal, is due to requirements of certain hydroelectric relicensing projects.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Includes depreciation expense associated with transportation equipment and finance lease assets of $10,277,057 and $6,579,550 during the three-month periods ended March 31, 2026 and 2025, respectively.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents proceeds (losses) from the disposal of fixed assets.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Weighted average remaining amortization period is approximately two years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Average amortization period is approximately one year.</link:footnote>
